// CRE Grade 2 (19 Nov 2026): the file had KICD outcomes only and no question families. 25 skills over the 22 sub-strands, each
// with two or more prerequisites (Grade 1 first: written as Grade 1 outcomes, they name the Grade 1 skill once Grade 1 is built),
// four misconceptions a child of seven really shows, and a teaching pack entry. Bible facts are those of the passages the KICD
// design names; nothing denominational is asked. Habits and performances (drawing, applying lessons, refusing gifts from
// strangers, sharing, obeying, honesty, thanking, forgiving, caring for items, chores, reciting) are marked by the teacher with the
// KICD rubric. NOTE for the reviewer: outcomes d to h of 'Creation of the sky, sun, moon, and stars' are learning experiences of a
// reading-the-Bible sub-strand that the text layer folded in; they stay word for word (official outcomes are never touched; their codes end x4 to
// x8), x4 is asked through READ_BIBLE and x5 to x8 go to the teacher. Lines that touch belief carry FAITH; child-safety lines carry SAFE.
// Merged by scripts/build-cre-grade.mjs 2. Draft until reviewed.
import { B, P, FAITH, RULE } from './common.mjs';

const SAFE = 'To confirm by a CRE teacher and the school counsellor (SAFE: child-safety content, read first): a common error of young children, not traced to a study by the author.';
const S = (sub, id, name, outcomes, forms, mastery, pre, mis, pack, rubric) => ({ sub, id, name, outcomes, forms, mastery: mastery + RULE, thinking: ['recall', 'reasoning'], pre, mis, pack, ...(rubric ? { rubric } : {}) });

